---
flowchart TD

  %% The canonical pd workflow on Claude Code's native features.
  %% Source of truth: docs/plans/2026-10-14-thin-pd-native-design.md §A2–§A5 (decisions D7–D16).

  %% ===================== ENTRY =====================
  subgraph ENTRY ["Work arrives"]
    direction LR
    IDEA["<b>Idea</b><br/>no settled problem"]
    REQ["<b>Feature request</b><br/>intent stated, behaviour implicit"]
    BUG["<b>Bug</b><br/>something broke"]
  end

  TRI{{"<b>0 · Triage</b> · /pd:secretary<br/>picks the depth: <b>standard</b> · <b>small</b> (an estimate: ≤ 3 tasks) · <b>express</b><br/>always standard for security, migrations, many files, areas new to the codebase<br/>risk tags: security · migration"}}
  IDEA --> TRI
  REQ --> TRI
  BUG --> TRI

  %% ===================== SPINE =====================
  CLAR["<b>1 · Clarify</b> &nbsp; <i>a brainstorm or rca item</i><br/>is this the right problem? what would success look like?<br/>research-fanout only when it pays · rca-fanout for every bug<br/><i>kills: the wrong problem</i>"]
  TRI -- "idea · bug" --> CLAR

  CRIT["<b>2 · Criteria</b> &nbsp; <i>specify</i><br/>shape.md ## Requirements<br/>goals · non-goals · user stories<br/>behaviour expectations B1…Bn, each with an observable outcome<br/><i>kills: what counts as done</i>"]
  CLAR --> CRIT
  TRI -- "request" --> CRIT

  G2{{"<b>gate</b> · phase-gate specify (exit)<br/>every expectation: id and observable outcome<br/>your sign-off recorded"}}
  R2{{"<b>calvin</b> · ≤ 3 review-revise rounds<br/>are the criteria faithful, and enough?<br/><b>you sign off the criteria</b>"}}
  CRIT --> R2 --> G2

  CON["<b>3 · Contracts</b> &nbsp; <i>design</i><br/>shape.md ## Design<br/><b>architecture diagram</b>: modules · flows · one contract per edge<br/>each contract pinned once · invariants<br/>test strategy: fixture locations · fakes · real resources allowed<br/>documents only: no code yet<br/><i>kills: what crosses each boundary</i>"]
  G2 --> CON

  G3{{"<b>gate</b> · phase-gate design<br/>diagram and test strategy present · no restated contract"}}
  R3{{"<b>design review</b> · Codex first · ≤ 3 review-revise cycles<br/>re-review checks only the earlier findings<br/>every edge has a contract, every contract an edge"}}
  CON --> G3 --> R3

  PLAN["<b>4 · Plan</b> &nbsp; <i>create-plan</i><br/>plan.md: per task · contract · test cases · proving command · file set<br/>test cases in plain words or pseudo code, citing B-ids,<br/>naming their fixture, edges included<br/>from_shape: goes stale when shape.md moves<br/><i>kills: order, and what proves each step</i>"]
  R3 --> PLAN

  G4{{"<b>gate</b> · pd-lint<br/>every task: test cases, proving command, files<br/>every B-id covered · from_shape: still matches"}}
  PLAN --> G4

  R4{{"<b>test-case review</b> · Codex first · ≤ 3 review-revise cycles<br/>faithful to the expectations? edges covered?"}}
  G4 --> R4

  %% ===================== EXECUTE =====================
  subgraph EXEC ["5 · Execute — implement-tasks workflow &nbsp; (kills: does the code meet each contract?)"]
    direction LR
    T1["task agent · sonnet · own worktree<br/>first commit: the tests + raising stubs<br/>then a commit per meaningful step"]
    T2["task agent · sonnet · own worktree<br/>first commit: the tests + raising stubs<br/>then a commit per meaningful step"]
    T3["sequential tasks · sonnet · own worktree<br/>one at a time, after the parallel ones land<br/>same commit rules"]
    MRG["<b>merger</b><br/>merges in plan order · per task:<br/>pd-proof · first commit: each test fails as a test,<br/>any already green is named<br/>HEAD passes · tests untouched · fixtures in place<br/>after each merge: all merged proofs re-run<br/>an unexpected result is re-run once"]
    T1 --> MRG
    T2 --> MRG
    T3 --> MRG
  end
  R4 --> T1
  R4 --> T2
  R4 --> T3

  %% ===================== VERIFY =====================
  subgraph VER ["6 · Verify — verify-change workflow &nbsp; (kills: does the whole change hold together?)"]
    direction LR
    REV["<b>code review</b> · Codex first · one pass<br/>correctness, criteria, over-engineering<br/>each test asserts its case (case map)"]
    QA["<b>QA</b> · strongest model<br/>runs the suites, drives the flows<br/>hunts the cases no criterion named<br/>asks what each criterion still allows"]
    FIX["<b>fixer</b> · ≤ 3 cycles<br/>each cycle judged by re-running the checks<br/>a judgement finding: the finder states the case,<br/>the fixer commits its test first,<br/>the QA re-run checks red, then green"]
    REV --> FIX
    QA --> FIX
  end
  MRG --> REV
  MRG --> QA

  FIN["<b>7 · Finish</b> &nbsp; <i>finish</i><br/>security review when tagged risk: security<br/>metrics entry in log.md · retro only on a trigger<br/>lessons become checks · merge to the base branch<br/><i>kills: what this taught</i>"]
  FIX --> FIN
  SHIP([Ship])
  FIN --> SHIP

  %% ===================== SHORTER PATHS =====================
  SMALL["<b>small</b>: Contracts and Plan<br/>written in one sitting<br/>one review call checks both"]
  EXP["<b>express</b>: a mini-spec<br/>stands in for stages 2–4<br/>each skip recorded<br/>verify: proof + QA battery"]
  TRI -. "small" .-> SMALL
  SMALL -.-> CON
  TRI -. "express" .-> EXP
  EXP -.-> T3

  %% ===================== STOPS =====================
  STOP[/"<b>stop and ask you</b><br/>in the main session · blocked beats guessed<br/>also at the token cap, or no progress: continue or stop?<br/>at a cap, first written down: deferred · follow-ups · decisions · assumptions"/]
  R2 -. "blockers left after 3 rounds" .-> STOP
  R3 -. "blockers left after 3 cycles" .-> STOP
  R4 -. "blockers left after 3 cycles" .-> STOP
  FIX -. "still failing after 3 cycles" .-> STOP
  MRG -. "check fails:<br/>fix cycle 1 on sonnet<br/>cycles 2–3 on strongest" .-> T1

  %% ===================== BACKWARD =====================
  R3 -. "criteria unbuildable" .-> CRIT
  QA -. "a case no criterion named" .-> CRIT
  REV -. "the contract was wrong" .-> CON
  MRG -. "task under-specified,<br/>or a test case wrong" .-> PLAN
  FIN -. "security blocker" .-> FIX

  %% ===================== RUNTIME =====================
  subgraph RUN ["How it runs"]
    direction LR
    COND["<b>Conductor</b> · main session<br/>asks you · writes the files<br/>launches the fan-out workflows<br/>dispatches single reviewers"]
    AUTO["<b>Unattended</b><br/>/goal keeps it going<br/>a Stop-hook script decides done<br/>yields while a workflow runs<br/>caps on depth · tokens"]
    FILES["<b>State</b> · committed files<br/>README.md frontmatter · log.md<br/>shape.md · plan.md · retro.md"]
    COND ~~~ AUTO ~~~ FILES
  end
  SHIP ~~~ RUN

  %% ===================== STYLE =====================
  classDef stage fill:#eef4fb,stroke:#3c6ea5,stroke-width:2px,color:#12263a
  classDef verify fill:#e6f0fa,stroke:#1f4e79,stroke-width:3px,color:#0d1f33
  classDef review fill:#fdf2e3,stroke:#c98a1b,stroke-width:2px,color:#4a3208
  classDef mech fill:#eaf6ec,stroke:#3f8c4f,stroke-width:2px,color:#123018
  classDef worker fill:#f4f1f8,stroke:#7a5fa3,stroke-width:1.5px,color:#2b1f3d
  classDef entry fill:#ffffff,stroke:#888,stroke-width:1.5px,color:#222
  classDef path fill:#ffffff,stroke:#888,stroke-width:1.5px,stroke-dasharray:5 4,color:#333
  classDef done fill:#3f8c4f,stroke:#2c6339,stroke-width:2px,color:#ffffff
  classDef stop fill:#fbeaea,stroke:#a8423f,stroke-width:2px,color:#3d1211
  classDef run fill:#f7f7f2,stroke:#777,stroke-width:1.5px,color:#222

  class CLAR,CRIT,CON,PLAN,FIN stage
  class QA verify
  class R2,R3,R4,REV review
  class TRI,G2,G3,G4 mech
  class T1,T2,T3,MRG,FIX worker
  class IDEA,REQ,BUG entry
  class SMALL,EXP path
  class SHIP done
  class STOP stop
  class COND,AUTO,FILES run
